<title>UK: Midlands will borrow to pay windfall tax.</title>
<headline>Midlands will borrow to pay windfall tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Midlands Electricity said on Wednesday the windfall tax announced in Labour's budget would cost it 130 million pounds and the company would have to borrow money to pay for it.</p>
<p>&quot;We calculated our share ... at around 130 million pounds. We can borrow money so that we can afford it, we can't afford it in terms of being able to support the investments we'd hoped to make,&quot; chief executive Mike Hughes said.</p>
<p>He said the company had showed their financial figures to the Treasury before the budget and were really disappointed they did not take any great notice.</p>
<p>He said the company was surprised by the amount of the windfall tax that would fall on electricity companies.</p>
<p>Investment would fall, he added.</p>
</text>
